---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import {
  siteConfig,
  homeUrl,
  siteHost,
  renderTemplate,
  legalUpdatedLabel,
} from '../lib/site';

const { appName, contactDisplay: contact } = siteConfig;

const sections = [
  { id: 'publisher', label: 'Publisher' },
  { id: 'no-video', label: 'No video on this site' },
  { id: 'availability', label: 'Availability and rights' },
  { id: 'installation-risk', label: 'Installation risk' },
  { id: 'external-links', label: 'External links' },
  { id: 'contact', label: 'Contact' },
];
---

<LegalLayout
  title={siteConfig.pages.disclaimer.title}
  description={renderTemplate(siteConfig.pages.disclaimer.description)}
  heading="Disclaimer"
  lede="What this page is, what it is not, and the limits that apply to the information here."
  updated={legalUpdatedLabel}
  sections={sections}
>
  <h2 id="publisher">Publisher</h2>
  <p>
    {siteHost} is the download page for the {appName} Android app, run by its publisher. The site
    is not operated, endorsed, sponsored or approved by any league, team, club, broadcaster or
    streaming platform.
  </p>
  <p>
    Team names, competition names, trademarks and logos belong to their respective owners. Any
    reference on this site is descriptive and does not imply affiliation or endorsement.
  </p>

  <h2 id="no-video">No video on this site</h2>
  <p>
    This website does not host, store, transmit or provide access to live video, recorded video,
    channels or feeds. It does not sell subscriptions, accounts or access codes. It publishes the
    APK we build and explains how to install it.
  </p>
  <p>
    What plays inside the app comes from the sources the app opens. Descriptions of sports
    categories refer to how the app is organised, not to a promise that a particular match,
    competition or channel is available.
  </p>

  <h2 id="availability">Availability and rights</h2>
  <p>
    Broadcast rights are territorial and time-limited. An event available in one country may not be
    available in another, and schedules change without notice. Availability inside the app depends
    on the providers behind each stream and on your region.
  </p>
  <p>
    You are responsible for using the app only for content you are entitled to access and for
    following the terms of the services you use. This page does not provide regional workarounds or
    instructions for bypassing restrictions.
  </p>

  <h2 id="installation-risk">Installation risk</h2>
  <p>
    Installing an Android APK from outside an app store carries risk. Files can be modified,
    replaced, or bundled with unwanted software. Download from the file linked on this page,
    compare the file details shown by your browser, review the permissions Android lists, and use
    your own security tools if you are unsure.
  </p>
  <p>
    No app can be guaranteed free of defects or malicious behaviour. You install and use the app at
    your own risk. This site is not responsible for damage to a device, loss of data, or loss arising
    from the app or from a third-party download host.
  </p>

  <h2 id="external-links">External links</h2>
  <p>
    Links to external download hosts and other sites are provided for convenience. Those sites are
    outside this site’s control, and their content, terms and privacy practices may change. A link
    does not imply endorsement.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Published site details are on the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>. The address shown there
    is <a href={homeUrl}>{contact}</a>; selecting it returns to the homepage. For rights matters,
    use the <a href="/dmca/">DMCA and takedown page</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
